  "title": "how a claim only Windows can settle gets checked and written down",
  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "Q1 of this plan — the last open question; constrained by IDEA.md's rule that every claim is checked on the real machine and by there being no automated route to it",
  "explanation": "The arrow that decides this is the one on the right: the verify stage reads the plan, not the conversation, so a result that only ever exists in a chat message is a check that did not happen as far as the gate is concerned. That is what separates [the three places](#three-places) — not how convenient they are to produce, but whether a later stage can find them. Leaves out which specific claims need a Windows check; that list is the watch rows, and it is still growing.",
